Z||000000||Lloyd Shelhamer||01-31-2001||03:36 PM||||Greetings from germany.<BR>I have a chance to buy a fiero GT with 3.4 l. engine. The crank is bad and parts are very scarce over here. I was able to find a 2.8 l engine complete and in good shape, but I need to know if I can install the smaller engine without having to change a lot of other things like exhaust or wiring.Any help will greatly appreciated.<BR>Thanks<P>Lloyd||||reg||1
Z||000001||Hank is Here||01-31-2001||04:51 PM||||Lloyd, <BR>First Welcome!<BR>The 2.8 that you found does it have aluminum heads or iron. The Fiero uses the iron heads.  If it is aluminum you can use the heads off the 3.4 on the 2.8 to make it work.  But yes eveything should be the same.  The 2.8 and 3.4 are in the same family of engines.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||ironhedno3||01-31-2001||07:29 PM||||if this 2.8 does have aluminum heads and you put the iron heads on it it wont have enough compression..3.1 and 3.4 uses the same crank..i work for an engine builder and if your interested in a new short block let me know||||reg||1
